A block is a group around the messages written inside it, nested blocks
included. A block's group spans all its sections, and each else, and or option
section is also a group of its own that names its block's line. Groups are
listed by line, outer before inner.
-- base/a.go --
package a

func A() {}

func B() {}
-- head/a.go --
package a

func A() { B() }

func B() { println() }
-- review.md --
---
frame: map
---
# Flow

```mermaid after
sequenceDiagram
  participant a as A
  participant b as B
  rect rgb(40, 40, 60)
    a->>b: calls B
    %% stop: a.go:3-3
    alt b is ready
      loop every line
        b->>b: prints
        %% stop: a.go:5-5
      end
    else b is busy
      b-->>a: busy
    end
  end
  par to the log
    a->>b: logs
  and to the screen
    a->>b: shows
  end
  opt on failure
    b--xa: fails
  end
  break when a stops
    a->>a: stops
  end
  alt a is ready
    alt b is ready
      a->>b: sends
    end
    a->>a: waits
  else a is busy
    a->>a: drops
  end
```

